  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 33. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. キャンセル — 申し込みや予約などを取り消すこと。\n2. キャンドル — 芯に火をつけて明かりをともすろうそく。\n3. キャンバス — 油絵などを描くために使う厚手の布。\n4. キャンパス — 大学などの建物が集まる敷地。\n5. キャンピングカー — 中で寝泊まりできる設備を備えた車。\n6. キャンプ — テントなどを使って野外で過ごすこと。\n7. 休暇 — 仕事や学校などを一定期間休むこと。\n8. 救急箱 — けがの手当てなどに使う物をまとめた箱。\n9. 休業 — 仕事や店の営業を休むこと。\n10. 休憩 — 活動の途中で少し休むこと。\n11. 休憩所 — 休むために用意された場所。\n12. 休校 — 学校の授業などを休みにすること。\n13. 休止 — しばらくの間やめること。\n14. 吸収 — 水や栄養などを中に取り込むこと。\n15. 救出 — 危険な場所から人などを助け出すこと。\n16. 休日 — 仕事や授業などが休みの日。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\nDo not add numerical claims, prices, quantities, currency denominations, calorie values or stroke-order numbers unless explicitly required by the target word. Mathematical concepts should have neutral concrete examples without unverified numeric diagrams.\n",
